    "path": "/contentPages/0",
    "raw": "by K'arn Hollowbeak, Avian scholar\nIt is common for some of the richest Avians to be buried with their worldly possessions. I have always found this a strange practise, but it transpires that many other species do the same. As a historian, it seems a shame to me to seal away sometimes-unique items, but I do also see the romanticism in being able to take your treasured things into the afterlife.",
    "value": "翼族学者 卡恩·空喙 撰\n翼族富者多携珍品入墓，视为通往彼岸之资。我初观此俗，甚觉怪诞，然考诸万族，方知此非我族独有。然作为治史之人，见独特器物永埋幽壤，实为惋惜。然细思之，逝者欲携心爱之物共赴来世，亦蕴含诗意之情怀。"
  },
  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/contentPages/1",
    "raw": "However, because of this trend, Avian tombs are often the targets of robbery, hence the employment of Tombkeepers, individuals who dedicate their lives to living in the tombs for a period of no less than ten years.",
    "value": "惜此风盛行，致我族陵墓屡遭贼人窥伺。故设陵墓守卫之职，择志士居墓守灵，任期不下十载，以护先民永世安宁。"
